"""
for c in cs:
    html += f"      <tr><td>{c['segment']}</td><td>{fmt_int(c['customers'])}</td><td>{fmt_pct(c['customer_share'])}</td><td>{fmt_money2(c['revenue'])}</td><td>{fmt_pct(c['revenue_share'])}</td><td>{fmt_money2(c['avg_revenue_per_cust'])}</td></tr>\n"

cs_1 = next(c for c in cs if c['segment']=='1 order')
cs_23 = next(c for c in cs if c['segment']=='2-3 orders')
cs_45 = next(c for c in cs if c['segment']=='4-5 orders')

html += f"""    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Customer value leverage.</strong>
  <ul class="insight-list">
    <li>One-time buyers make up <strong>{fmt_pct(cs_1['customer_share'])}</strong> of the customer base but contribute only <strong>{fmt_pct(cs_1['revenue_share'])}</strong> of revenue — converting even a fraction of these to repeat buyers is the single largest growth lever.</li>
    <li>The 2–3 order segment — <strong>{fmt_pct(cs_23['customer_share'])}</strong> of customers — drives <strong>{fmt_pct(cs_23['revenue_share'])}</strong> of revenue at {fmt_money2(cs_23['avg_revenue_per_cust'])} per customer. This is the core repeat-buyer cohort; protect it with loyalty/retention programs.</li>
    <li>The 4+ order "high-frequency" cohort ({fmt_int(cs_45['customers']+cs['customers']*0)} customers in 4–5 order band, {fmt_int(cs[-1]['customers'])} in 6+) is small but carries disproportionate LTV — prioritize for VIP treatment.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<!-- CLOSING -->
<h2 class="section">Strategic Recommendations for FY Planning</h2>
<div class="card">
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Revisit the discount playbook.</strong> Current flat-% discounts erode AOV without lifting quantity. Pilot bundle/threshold mechanics in Q1 to measure true incremental volume.</li>
    <li><strong>Close the store-performance gap.</strong> Pair bottom-quartile stores with top-quartile peers and audit assortment, staffing, and local promotion alignment.</li>
    <li><strong>Reactivate one-time buyers.</strong> The single-order cohort ({fmt_pct(cs_1['customer_share'])} of customers) is the largest addressable reactivation pool — pilot a winback program measuring second-order conversion.</li>
    <li><strong>Range-review bottom SKUs.</strong> The bottom-5 products deserve a "fix, replace, or delist" decision within the first quarter of the new fiscal year.</li>
    <li><strong>Enrich the analytics foundation.</strong> Joining product, store, and customer dimension tables into the analytics fact would unlock brand/category/cocoa-% views, geographic comparisons, and loyalty-member ROI — all explicitly deferred in this report due to missing dimension data.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

